I've fixed issues 3, 6, and 8, and left everything else untouched. Both `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` pass.

## What I changed

**Issue 3 — typos/old links landed on the login screen instead of a 404.** The request-handling middleware (`proxy.ts`) was redirecting *every* unknown path to `/login` for logged-out visitors, so a real 404 could never appear. I inverted the logic to only require sign-in for the actual private pages (dashboard, units, tenants, cheques, buildings, calendar, network, settings) plus non-public API routes; anything else falls through. I added a proper `app/not-found.tsx` that renders a styled "page not found" and returns a real 404 (Next auto-marks it `noindex`). Bonus: `/privacy` and `/terms`, which were also wrongly bouncing to login, are now reachable.

**Issue 6 — 17 preloaded font files + an off-screen image ahead of the hero.** The homepage defaults to English but was preloading both Arabic-script fonts (Tajawal, IBM Plex Sans Arabic) that only appear after a manual language toggle — I set `preload: false` on those (they still load on demand). I added `loading="lazy"` to the below-the-fold dashboard screenshot so it no longer competes with the hero, and marked the hero skyline `fetchPriority="high"`.

**Issue 8 — fake footer links.** "Blog", "Security", and "About Ganaken" pointed at in-page anchors, but no such pages exist. Creating them would be issues 2 and 4 (out of my scope) and would mean fabricating content, so per the rules I removed the three misleading links rather than fake destinations. Careers/Contact (email) and Privacy/Terms (real pages) remain.

## One thing to flag on the build

The build initially failed while pre-rendering `/calendar` with a Supabase "URL and API key are required" error. I confirmed this is **pre-existing and unrelated to my edits** — it reproduces identically on a clean tree with my changes stashed. The cause is that this sandbox is missing the public `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` variables (real deploys supply them). I did **not** touch any `.env` file; I supplied those variables inline for the single verification build (real URL from the existing `SUPABASE_URL`, placeholder anon key just so the client can instantiate during pre-render), and the build completed cleanly — `/_not-found` registered as a static 404, everything else intact. So `BUILD=OK` reflects that my changes compile and build in the environment the app is actually configured for.

I did not commit or push — that's left to the script.
